State "=== work-queue re-drive / close-contention ===".
State "workers-first ordering: w1+w2+w3 are genuinely blocked in DrainUntil when producer closes work".

Pull a rabbit.
    Define work as a channel of number.
    Define results as a channel of number.
    Define n as 30.

    Have rabbit start a task as worker-1:
        Define count-1 as 0.
        Define job as the delivery from work.
        While job is not void, repeat:
            Define v as (job but void is 0).
            Send (v * 2) through results.
            Increment count-1 by 1.
            The job becomes the delivery from work.
        Done.
        State "worker-1: processed {count-1} items".
    Done.

    Have rabbit start a task as worker-2:
        Define count-2 as 0.
        Define job as the delivery from work.
        While job is not void, repeat:
            Define v as (job but void is 0).
            Send (v * 2) through results.
            Increment count-2 by 1.
            The job becomes the delivery from work.
        Done.
        State "worker-2: processed {count-2} items".
    Done.

    Have rabbit start a task as worker-3:
        Define count-3 as 0.
        Define job as the delivery from work.
        While job is not void, repeat:
            Define v as (job but void is 0).
            Send (v * 2) through results.
            Increment count-3 by 1.
            The job becomes the delivery from work.
        Done.
        State "worker-3: processed {count-3} items".
    Done.

    Have rabbit start a task as producer:
        Define i as 1.
        While i is n or less, repeat:
            Send i through work.
            The i becomes the i + 1.
        Done.
        Close work.
        State "producer: sent {n} items, closed work channel".
    Done.

    Have rabbit start a task as collector:
        Define received as a series of number.
        Define got as the delivery from results.
        While got is not void, repeat:
            Insert (got but void is 0) into received.
            If (the number of received) is n, Stop.
            The got becomes the delivery from results.
        Done.
        Define actual-sum as 0.
        For each r in received, increment actual-sum by r.
        Define expected-sum as n * (n + 1).
        State "collector: received {the number of received} results".
        State "expected sum: {expected-sum}".
        State "actual sum:   {actual-sum}".
        If actual-sum is expected-sum, state "correctness: PASS (all 30 items processed exactly once)".
        If actual-sum is not expected-sum, state "correctness: FAIL".
    Done.
Done.

State "".
State "=== Done. reached - all 5 tasks terminated cleanly ===".
